The dataset in this directory — the rules, thresholds, quotes, retrieval dates,
histories, notices, statements and readings in dataset.json, countries.json,
exclusions.md and the verification checklists — is licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence.

Copyright (c) 2026 Oytun

You are free to share and adapt this dataset for any purpose, including
commercially, on one condition: attribution. Credit the dataset, link to its
source repository, indicate whether you changed it, and link to this licence.
You may do so in any reasonable manner, but not in a way that suggests the
licensor endorses you or your use.

A sufficient attribution line:

    Work-permit rules dataset by Oytun (https://github.com/<org>/<repo>),
    licensed CC BY 4.0. Changes: <none | describe>.

Full legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
Human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

What this licence does not cover
--------------------------------

The verbatim quotes in this dataset are short excerpts of official texts —
statutes, regulations and administrative information published by public
authorities — reproduced for the purpose of citing the rule they state. Each
carries the URL it was read from and the date. The licence above applies to the
dataset as a compiled and annotated work; it does not claim rights over the
official texts themselves, whose terms are noted in ../NOTICE.

countries.json was derived from Unicode CLDR region data and hand-edited; the
Unicode licence and its attribution requirement are also recorded in ../NOTICE.
